# ⚙️ General AVR Compilation Steps

The following steps are used to compile and program an Embedded C program for the **ATmega328P**.

The complete process is:

```text
C Source Code
     ↓
avr-gcc
     ↓
ELF File
     ↓
avr-objcopy
     ↓
HEX File
     ↓
avrdude
     ↓
ATmega328P Flash

1️⃣ Write the Embedded C Program
Create your C source file:
nano blink.c

Example:
#include <avr/io.h>

int main(void)
{
    DDRB |= (1 << PB5);

    while (1)
    {
        PORTB |= (1 << PB5);
    }
}

2️⃣ Compile the C Program
Use avr-gcc to compile the program for the ATmega328P:
avr-gcc -mmcu=atmega328p -Os -o blink.elf blink.c

🔍 Command Breakdown
Option	Purpose
avr-gcc	AVR C compiler
-mmcu=atmega328p	Specifies the target microcontroller
-Os	Optimizes the program for smaller size
-o blink.elf	Specifies the output ELF file
blink.c	Input C source file


The result is:
blink.elf

3️⃣ Convert ELF to HEX
Convert the ELF file into Intel HEX format using avr-objcopy:
avr-objcopy -O ihex -R .eeprom blink.elf blink.hex

🔍 Command Breakdown
Option	Purpose
avr-objcopy	Converts the generated file format
-O ihex	Selects Intel HEX as the output format
-R .eeprom	Removes the EEPROM section
blink.elf	Input ELF file
blink.hex	Output HEX file


The result is:
blink.hex

4️⃣ Check the Program Size
You can check how much Flash and RAM the program uses:
avr-size blink.elf

Example:
   text    data     bss     dec     hex
    120       0       0     120      78

5️⃣ Connect the ATmega328P
Connect the ATmega328P to your programmer or development board.

For an Arduino Uno, the USB serial device may appear as:
/dev/ttyACM0

You can check available serial ports using:
ls /dev/ttyACM*

6️⃣ Upload the HEX File
For an ATmega328P using an Arduino-style bootloader:
avrdude -p m328p -c arduino -P /dev/ttyACM0 -b 115200 -U flash:w:blink.hex:i

🔍 Command Breakdown
Option	Purpose
avrdude	AVR programming utility
-p m328p	Target device: ATmega328P
-c arduino	Arduino bootloader protocol
-P /dev/ttyACM0	Serial communication port
-b 115200	Baud rate
-U	Performs a memory operation
flash	Target Flash memory
w	Write operation
blink.hex	HEX file to upload
i	Intel HEX format


7️⃣ Complete Workflow
For a program called blink.c:
📝 Source Code
blink.c

🔨 Compile
avr-gcc -mmcu=atmega328p -Os -o blink.elf blink.c

🔄 Convert
avr-objcopy -O ihex -R .eeprom blink.elf blink.hex

📊 Check Size
avr-size blink.elf

🚀 Upload
avrdude -p m328p -c arduino -P /dev/ttyACM0 -b 115200 -U flash:w:blink.hex:i

🎯 Summary
blink.c
   │
   │ avr-gcc
   ↓
blink.elf
   │
   │ avr-objcopy
   ↓
blink.hex
   │
   │ avrdude
   ↓
ATmega328P Flash
   │
   ↓
Program Execution

🧰 Tools Used
- avr-gcc → Compiles the Embedded C program
- avr-objcopy → Converts ELF to HEX
- avr-size → Displays program memory usage
- avrdude → Uploads the HEX file to the ATmega328P
